1
00:00:00,179 --> 00:00:05,087
Ever notice your lower back feels stiffer after a long commute than after an actual workout?

2
00:00:05,714 --> 00:00:10,183
Sitting compresses spinal discs and slows blood flow - certain foods make it worse.

3
00:00:10,764 --> 00:00:15,583
Salty snacks, alcohol, and sugary treats are three common culprits.

4
00:00:15,983 --> 00:00:21,829
A bag of chips or fast food can pack in over half a day's sodium, and extra sodium may cause fluid retention.

5
00:00:22,149 --> 00:00:25,463
Air-popped popcorn satisfies the craving with far less salt.

6
00:00:25,863 --> 00:00:30,402
Several drinks after work can dehydrate you and hurt your sleep, cutting into muscle recovery.

7
00:00:30,722 --> 00:00:33,800
Water plus a banana before bed helps offset that.

8
00:00:34,200 --> 00:00:37,632
Sugary soda and pastries cause quick blood sugar swings that may fuel inflammation.

9
00:00:37,952 --> 00:00:39,765
Sparkling water or fruit works instead.

10
00:00:40,280 --> 00:00:43,905
Cutting back on sodium, alcohol, and sugar is a simple place to start.
